  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1259 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nDry and hot conditions will persist across West Central Texas \nthrough the upcoming week. The upper high will be positioned over \nnorth central Texas on Monday and will migrate slowly westward to \nthe Four Corners region by late in the week. Daytime highs through\nthe week will range from the mid and upper 90s along the I-10 \ncorridor, and between 100 and 104 degrees across the Concho \nValley, Heartland and Big Country. Overnight lows will be in the \n70s. By late in the week, the GFS shows a short wave moving \nsoutheast through the central Plains, with a possible cold front \npushing through Oklahoma into north Texas. However, confidence \nregarding this scenario remains quite low at this time.",
